---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="1Password in Blanc — Built-in Login Fill on macOS"
  description="Use your existing 1Password logins in Blanc on macOS. Set up the optional built-in integration and fill a matching login when you ask."
  path="/features/1password"
  page="feature-1password"
  current="features"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline slot="head">
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://blancbrowser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Features","item":"https://blancbrowser.com/features"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"1Password","item":"https://blancbrowser.com/features/1password"}]}
</script>
<main class="feature-page feature-detail-page">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/features">features</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">1Password</span></nav>
  <section class="feature-hero feature-hero--detail feature-hero--text" aria-labelledby="onepassword-title">
    <p class="section-kicker">1Password · macOS</p>
    <h1 id="onepassword-title">Keep your 1Password logins close.</h1>
    <p>Use the logins you already keep in 1Password. Blanc’s built-in macOS integration fills a matching Login item from your installed desktop app when you ask.</p>
    <p class="feature-availability">Requires the 1Password desktop app and account. Off by default. Currently available on macOS only.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="#onepassword-setup">Set up login fill <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
  </section>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid" id="onepassword-setup" aria-labelledby="onepassword-setup-title">
    <div><p class="section-kicker">a one-time setup</p><h2 id="onepassword-setup-title">Connect the app you already use.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>1. Enable the connection in 1Password.</h3><p>Install the 1Password desktop app and sign in. Open Settings → Developer. Under <strong>Integrate with the 1Password SDKs</strong>, enable <strong>Integrate with other apps</strong>.</p></article>
      <article><h3>2. Enable login fill in Blanc.</h3><p>Open Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → 1Password. Turn on <strong>Fill logins from 1Password</strong>, enter the email address you use to sign in to 1Password or your account ID, and choose <strong>Verify</strong>. Approve Blanc Browser when 1Password asks.</p></article>
      <article><h3>3. Fill when you need it.</h3><p>On a website login form, press <kbd>⌥⌘P</kbd> (Option + Command + P), or choose View → Fill Login from 1Password. If several Login items match the site, choose the one you want. You can also run <code>/1password</code> from the Island.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="onepassword-choice-title">
    <div><p class="section-kicker">you choose when</p><h2 id="onepassword-choice-title">A hint at the form. Fill on request.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>A shortcut beside your browsing.</h3><p>Once configured, the Island can show a key hint on a page with a visible current-password field. Choose it to start the same login-fill flow.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Your passwords stay in 1Password.</h3><p>Blanc never fills automatically or saves the returned credentials. The setting and account identifier stay on this device and are excluded from Sync. <a href="/privacy">Read how login fill handles data.</a></p></article>
      <article><h3>Mac support today.</h3><p>The integration is currently available on macOS only. Windows and Linux builds do not offer 1Password login fill. It fills matching Login items; it does not provide password saving, payment-card filling, or 1Password passkeys.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="feature-close" aria-labelledby="onepassword-close-title"><p class="section-kicker">ready when you are</p><h2 id="onepassword-close-title">Bring your logins to Blanc on Mac.</h2><a class="cta" href="/download">Download Blanc</a></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
